<title>LEBANON: Lebanon has $105.1 mln payments surplus in August. [CORRECTED 15:50 GMT]</title>
<headline>Lebanon has $105.1 mln payments surplus in August. [CORRECTED 15:50 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects figure in headline and first paragraph to $105.1 million from $105.5 million)</p>
<p>Lebanon had a $105.1 million balance of payments surplus in August, $36.9 million (corrects from $36.5 million) down on July but well above the August 1995 surplus of $30 million, the Bank of Lebanon said in its latest monthly bulletin on Monday.</p>
<p>    BALANCE OF PAYMENTS	August 96     July 96    August 95</p>
<p>    Monthly			105.1	   142.0	  30.0</p>
<p>    Year to date		 285.6	   180.5	-216.9</p>
<p>Annual results</p>
<p>    1995	 256</p>
<p>    1994     1,130.5</p>
<p>    1993     1,169.5</p>
<p>Note - Figures in millions of U.S. dollars</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 353078 861723</p>
